I'm using `CycloneDX 6.2.0` with `Cake.CycloneDX 0.0.5` to scan a C# project file but I see in the terminal that "The following orphaned packages have been removed" and a list of all direct projects and nugets that my project depend on.
The output file contain only the metadata node and zero items in the components node.

The CdxDotNetSettings that used in the Cake Frosting task:
``` C#
var settings = new CdxDotNetSettings
{
    ComponentType = CdxComponentClassification.Library,
    ComponentName = projectName,
    ComponentVersion = projectVersion,
    IncludeProjectReferences = includeProjectReferences,
    ExcludeDevelopmentDependencies = true,
    ExcludeTestProjects = true,
    Recursive = false,
    DisablePackageRestore = false,
    Output = outputFilePath.GetDirectory(),
    FileName = outputFilePath.GetFilename().FullPath,
    SpecVersion = CdxDotNetSpecificationVersion.V1_7,
    OutputFormat = CdxDotNetOutputFormat.Xml,
};

if (excludeFilters != null)
{
    foreach (var excludeFilter in excludeFilters)
    {
        settings.WithExcludeFilter(excludeFilter);
    }
}
context.CdxDotNet(projectFilePath, settings);
```

UPDATE:
Removing `settings.WithExcludeFilter(excludeFilter);` fixed the problem.
